  "equipment_type": "UPS (uninterruptible power supply)",
  "applies_to": "Liebert Series 600 UPS systems on Modbus, read by a BASgatewayLX.",
  "summary": "Gateway profile for the Liebert Series 600 UPS: 80 objects (42 AI, 38 BI), all polled. Binary inputs give load on inverter/bypass/battery, transfers, switch states and the alarm and customer alarm bits; analog inputs give nominal ratings, load in VA, W and % of capacity, frequencies, battery voltage, current, time and charge, and input, bypass and output voltages and currents per line.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "Built from Contemporary Controls' BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile LIEBERT_SERIES_600_UPS_a_LX.csv; the profile maps the registers in the Liebert Series 600 Modbus register list (https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/Liebert_IntelliSlot.docx).",
    "Object instances are the ones this profile assigns when it is loaded into the gateway. A site that edited or rebuilt the profile may use different instances.",
    "All 80 rows are flagged for polling in the profile, so every object is served to BACnet once the profile is loaded.",
    "The CSV has no read/write column: Analog/Binary Inputs are read-only and Analog/Binary Outputs are commandable (priority array), which is how the gateway maps them (access inferred). Descriptions give the Modbus register each object reads.",
    "Some names appear more than once in the profile as published (Load On Bypass); they are kept as printed and told apart by instance."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile LIEBERT_SERIES_600_UPS_a",
    "doc_number": "LIEBERT_SERIES_600_UPS_a_LX.csv",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/Liebert600UPS.zip"
  },
